WEBVTT

1
00:00:29.363 --> 00:00:30.447
Get him!

2
00:00:32.533 --> 00:00:33.367
Yay. fight!

3
00:00:35.077 --> 00:00:37.496
- Leave him alone!
- He called me a swear word.

4
00:00:37.829 --> 00:00:40.958
He's wearing the same clothes
as yesterday and he smells.

5
00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:42.793
You're a dick.

6
00:00:43.293 --> 00:00:44.670
Hey. man. Here.

7
00:00:45.295 --> 00:00:48.131
I can take care of myself.
You wanna go? Right now.

8
00:00:49.091 --> 00:00:49.925
Nah.

9
00:01:09.611 --> 00:01:11.613
- Where's your lunch?
- Already ate it.

10
00:01:11.697 --> 00:01:12.864
Out of the trash can!

11
00:01:12.948 --> 00:01:14.241
Shut up! I did not!

12
00:01:14.866 --> 00:01:15.867
Want a sandwich?

13
00:01:17.077 --> 00:01:17.953
No.

14
00:01:19.413 --> 00:01:21.915
Marisa made turkey. I hate turkey.

15
00:01:22.624 --> 00:01:23.500
Not hungry.

16
00:01:23.584 --> 00:01:27.129
Come on. take the sandwich.
And I'll take half your Twinkies.

17
00:01:29.131 --> 00:01:30.632
I don't got Twinkies.

18
00:01:36.179 --> 00:01:37.347
Hey. those are mine!

19
00:01:38.140 --> 00:01:39.391
And now they're his.

20
00:01:50.110 --> 00:01:51.820
I don't need you to stick up for me.

21
00:01:52.613 --> 00:01:54.781
I know. I just wanted a Twinkie.

22
00:01:55.741 --> 00:01:59.161
<i>Bryce and I have been friends
since the third grade.</i>

23
00:02:10.255 --> 00:02:11.465
<i>And friendship.</i>

24
00:02:12.341 --> 00:02:14.635
<i>it can be this really powerful thing.</i>

25
00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:17.763
- The fuck are you two doing?
- Just hold on.

26
00:02:17.846 --> 00:02:20.057
He's gonna keep doing it.
We have to stop him.

27
00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:21.892
- Not like this.
- I'm calling the cops.

28
00:02:21.975 --> 00:02:24.353
Just shut the fuck up and hold on. Bryce!

29
00:02:24.436 --> 00:02:27.064
It's never gonna get any better.
You were right to run away.

30
00:02:27.147 --> 00:02:28.148
No. I wasn't.

31
00:02:28.357 --> 00:02:30.651
That's why you came and got me.
remember?

32
00:02:30.734 --> 00:02:33.320
- For Jess. for Hannah.
- Hannah wants him dead.

33
00:02:33.487 --> 00:02:34.529
No. I don't think she does.

34
00:02:34.905 --> 00:02:37.324
I don't think she wants
to keep seeing people get hurt.

35
00:02:37.407 --> 00:02:39.368
I don't. Okay?

36
00:02:51.254 --> 00:02:52.923
This is fucking ridiculous.

37
00:02:54.466 --> 00:02:55.634
You're gonna go back inside

38
00:02:55.717 --> 00:02:57.886
and you're gonna pour yourself
another glass of whiskey.

39
00:02:57.969 --> 00:03:00.222
and you're gonna forget
that we were ever here. got it?

40
00:03:08.438 --> 00:03:10.816
I heard they just filed
for another additional witness.

41
00:03:11.066 --> 00:03:12.984
That wouldn't be you
by any chance. would it?

42
00:03:15.779 --> 00:03:17.906
You should be more scared
than you are. Justin.

43
00:03:19.616 --> 00:03:23.161
Bryce. I've got nothing left to lose.

44
00:03:24.830 --> 00:03:26.415
That makes me the dangerous one.

45
00:03:35.507 --> 00:03:36.341
What the fuck?

46
00:03:37.926 --> 00:03:38.760
What is it?

47
00:03:39.970 --> 00:03:40.929
We're being followed.

48
00:03:44.433 --> 00:03:45.475
Are you sure?

49
00:03:53.692 --> 00:03:54.526
We'll lose him.

50
00:03:55.068 --> 00:03:57.779
- Dude. it's a Prius.
- And I'm a fucking awesome driver.

51
00:04:12.544 --> 00:04:14.796
<i>And friendship is complicated.</i>

52
00:04:15.297 --> 00:04:19.092
<i>You find yourself doing things
you never thought you'd do.</i>

53
00:04:23.930 --> 00:04:24.765
We're clear.

54
00:04:25.515 --> 00:04:26.683
What the hell was that?

55
00:04:28.018 --> 00:04:29.895
Probably the person
fucking with all of us.

56
00:04:29.978 --> 00:04:31.855
- Bryce.
- It wasn't his car.

57
00:04:32.022 --> 00:04:33.106
Well. one of his boys.

58
00:04:34.065 --> 00:04:36.985
Because you're testifying. Tomorrow.

59
00:04:39.404 --> 00:04:42.282
You... You're really gonna do it. right?

60
00:04:44.785 --> 00:04:45.619
Yeah.

61
00:04:45.786 --> 00:04:48.622
<i>Because friendship.
you commit to it.</i>

62
00:04:49.206 --> 00:04:50.957
Alex?

63
00:04:51.041 --> 00:04:53.084
<i>No matter what.</i>

64
00:04:53.168 --> 00:04:54.002
Alex!

65
00:04:55.086 --> 00:04:55.921
Alex!

66
00:04:56.004 --> 00:04:57.297
What? I'm awake.

67
00:04:58.673 --> 00:04:59.508
Oh.

68
00:05:00.175 --> 00:05:01.676
- Hey. guys.
- "Hey. guys"?

69
00:05:02.052 --> 00:05:05.847
- Did you not hear us pounding on the door?
- I don't know. I must've fallen asleep.

70
00:05:05.931 --> 00:05:08.475
Alexander Dean Standall.

71
00:05:10.769 --> 00:05:11.603
What is this?

72
00:05:11.978 --> 00:05:14.940
Do you know the damage
these things can do to your health?

73
00:05:15.023 --> 00:05:17.692
The only damage they do
is to the roof of your mouth. Mom.

74
00:05:17.776 --> 00:05:19.528
Well. we're back to a healthy breakfast.

75
00:05:22.072 --> 00:05:23.365
Zach. you're welcome to join.

76
00:05:29.412 --> 00:05:30.872
What's the big emergency?

77
00:05:32.249 --> 00:05:34.042
This is what I woke up to this morning.

78
00:05:34.751 --> 00:05:36.628
12:12 a.m. "Someone gave me a bullet."

79
00:05:36.878 --> 00:05:38.922
12:13 a.m. "Someone gave me a gun."

80
00:05:39.005 --> 00:05:41.174
12:37 a.m. "I figured it all out."

81
00:05:41.466 --> 00:05:45.428
You can't fucking text shit like this
to a person and then fall asleep.

82
00:05:45.512 --> 00:05:48.181
Okay. I couldn't explain more
because my thumbs got tired.

83
00:05:48.348 --> 00:05:51.059
The last time you didn't respond
to my texts or calls. you...

84
00:05:53.270 --> 00:05:54.104
I know.

85
00:05:59.067 --> 00:06:02.445
So. what the hell is going on?

86
00:06:04.823 --> 00:06:06.366
I know who's messing with us.

87
00:06:10.245 --> 00:06:11.580
But I don't know where he is.

88
00:06:16.334 --> 00:06:17.460
Good morning.

89
00:06:19.421 --> 00:06:21.965
- Hey. Mom.
- Hey. Mrs. Jensen. Mr. Jensen.

90
00:06:22.048 --> 00:06:23.466
What the hell happened to you two?

91
00:06:23.925 --> 00:06:25.176
- It was a fight.
- Sports.

92
00:06:26.511 --> 00:06:29.889
Mine... mine was a fight
and his was sports.

93
00:06:29.973 --> 00:06:31.850
I told Dad yesterday. PE.

94
00:06:32.601 --> 00:06:35.312
If someone's hurting you.
we need to know what's going on.

95
00:06:35.395 --> 00:06:37.939
Wait. wha... What are you doing here?

96
00:06:39.316 --> 00:06:43.903
Well. um. I want to apologize

97
00:06:43.987 --> 00:06:47.866
that. uh. an argument that was largely
between your father and me

98
00:06:47.949 --> 00:06:49.951
had the impact it did on the family.

99
00:06:50.952 --> 00:06:52.037
And on you. Justin.

100
00:06:53.204 --> 00:06:54.039
It wasn't fair.

101
00:06:54.706 --> 00:06:57.667
I feel like I came here
and messed everything up. so...

102
00:06:57.751 --> 00:07:00.378
- No. No. it's not...
- Justin. that's not what happened.

103
00:07:00.754 --> 00:07:01.588
You didn't.

104
00:07:06.259 --> 00:07:09.220
So. you just... You're back?

105
00:07:11.222 --> 00:07:12.057
I'm back.

106
00:07:13.850 --> 00:07:15.977
And I need to speak to Justin privately.

107
00:07:17.270 --> 00:07:18.104
After breakfast.

108
00:07:20.023 --> 00:07:22.442
I heard last night
that you're going to testify today.

109
00:07:23.902 --> 00:07:29.783
And while I like Dennis Vasquez very much.
he does not represent your interests.

110
00:07:30.867 --> 00:07:34.412
I wanna make sure that you understand
everything that's at stake for you

111
00:07:34.496 --> 00:07:35.664
before you testify.

112
00:07:36.247 --> 00:07:38.208
What do you mean?
What's at stake?

113
00:07:39.960 --> 00:07:43.213
Clay. I don't want us to have secrets.
but if I'm going to help Justin.

114
00:07:43.296 --> 00:07:46.049
that has to be between the two of us...
for now.

115
00:07:47.008 --> 00:07:50.637
If he chooses to tell you after we talk.
that's up to him.

116
00:07:52.806 --> 00:07:53.723
Can you trust me?

117
00:07:59.688 --> 00:08:00.522
For now.

118
00:08:02.524 --> 00:08:05.485
- Well. what did she tell you?
- Nothing important.

119
00:08:05.568 --> 00:08:07.570
Just walked me through
how the day's gonna go.

120
00:08:08.780 --> 00:08:11.700
- What did she say was at stake?
- Mostly everything you already know.

121
00:08:12.742 --> 00:08:13.576
Damn it.

122
00:08:14.369 --> 00:08:16.162
- Do you know how to tie a tie?
- Yes.

123
00:08:17.414 --> 00:08:19.165
I'm just nervous. okay?

124
00:08:31.052 --> 00:08:31.970
Oh. I guess...

125
00:08:34.889 --> 00:08:37.767
...doing this sober
is a lot harder than I thought it'd be.

126
00:08:39.269 --> 00:08:43.148
And. you know. I'm gonna have to say stuff
about me and Hannah.

127
00:08:43.857 --> 00:08:46.943
Stuff that you don't... you don't know.

128
00:08:49.988 --> 00:08:54.034
We... We didn't.
We never had sex or anything like that.

129
00:08:55.660 --> 00:08:56.870
There's just more to the story.

130
00:09:00.957 --> 00:09:02.834
I don't want you to start hating me again.

131
00:09:09.340 --> 00:09:10.383
Who said I stopped?

132
00:09:16.431 --> 00:09:18.266
Just don't lose your shit. okay?

133
00:09:20.393 --> 00:09:22.145
Man. you really freaked me out last night.

134
00:09:27.817 --> 00:09:28.902
Where'd you get the gun?

135
00:09:32.906 --> 00:09:34.365
I borrowed it from a friend.

136
00:09:35.992 --> 00:09:36.826
Well. give it back.

137
00:09:38.703 --> 00:09:41.039
Yeah. No. yeah. for sure.

138
00:09:46.920 --> 00:09:49.798
Jesus. how do you not know how...?

139
00:09:49.881 --> 00:09:52.175
I've seen you in a tie.
Last year at the winter dance.

140
00:09:57.180 --> 00:09:58.890
Bryce used to tie them for me.

141
00:10:02.310 --> 00:10:03.686
I never really learned how.

142
00:10:05.897 --> 00:10:08.108
<i>I like the way
you're taking care of Justin.</i>

143
00:10:09.359 --> 00:10:11.528
He really is just a sweet. injured boy.

144
00:10:12.028 --> 00:10:13.696
Yeah. and girls are suckers for that.

145
00:10:15.949 --> 00:10:19.077
You know. we're also suckers
for the angry. vengeful hero types.

146
00:10:22.705 --> 00:10:24.165
I was gonna kill him. Hannah.

147
00:10:26.376 --> 00:10:27.418
I was ready to.

148
00:10:30.130 --> 00:10:31.047
But is Justin right?

149
00:10:34.926 --> 00:10:36.177
Is that not what you want?

150
00:10:38.263 --> 00:10:39.639
I want you to forgive me.

151
00:10:46.271 --> 00:10:49.149
But maybe that's the one thing
in the world you won't do for me.

152
00:10:52.193 --> 00:10:54.320
Your parents said we could drive together.

153
00:10:54.404 --> 00:10:57.365
And they'll be right behind us
in one of the other Priuses.

154
00:11:07.458 --> 00:11:08.293
Jensen.

155
00:11:16.009 --> 00:11:20.096
Look. I promise you. there's no box
of pictures or anything like that.

156
00:11:20.263 --> 00:11:23.182
This is just fucking Zach making shit up
to make me look bad.

157
00:11:23.474 --> 00:11:25.727
- What happened that night?
- It was your idea to have an audience.

158
00:11:25.810 --> 00:11:28.187
No one forced you to get stoned
out of your mind.

159
00:11:28.271 --> 00:11:30.064
I even warned you not to hit that shit.

160
00:11:30.315 --> 00:11:31.608
What about Hickman's Bridge?

161
00:11:33.443 --> 00:11:36.070
- I thought that was our place.
- Is that why you walked out?

162
00:11:36.321 --> 00:11:38.323
Jesus. Chlöe. seriously?

163
00:11:39.032 --> 00:11:42.493
It's not like I grill you about every guy
you hooked up with before me. do I?

164
00:11:42.577 --> 00:11:44.495
- Where's the trust?
- What was I supposed to do?

165
00:11:44.579 --> 00:11:47.081
Not walk out. Not testify against me.

166
00:11:47.749 --> 00:11:49.667
You thought that was gonna make you
feel better?

167
00:11:50.001 --> 00:11:52.170
Do you really think
anyone's gonna trust you after that?

168
00:11:55.465 --> 00:11:57.884
Okay.
time for disciplinary matters.

169
00:11:57.967 --> 00:12:00.428
If we're going to establish
a pattern of behavior.

170
00:12:00.678 --> 00:12:03.097
your testimony needs
to contradict his claim

171
00:12:03.181 --> 00:12:05.433
that he's never forced himself
on another student.

172
00:12:06.434 --> 00:12:07.268
Okay.

173
00:12:07.477 --> 00:12:09.979
It all comes down
to whether the jury believes you. so...

174
00:12:10.772 --> 00:12:14.025
Ms. Struhl is gonna do whatever she can
to discredit you on the cross.

175
00:12:14.317 --> 00:12:16.611
She's gonna bring up everything.
Do you understand?

176
00:12:19.113 --> 00:12:21.741
- Yeah. I understand.
- Justin. you can't do this halfway.

177
00:12:22.659 --> 00:12:24.911
If you leave them
any room to doubt you. they will.

178
00:12:25.161 --> 00:12:26.496
Bryce fooled them yesterday.

179
00:12:28.581 --> 00:12:30.583
Yeah. I'll do my best. Mrs. Baker.

180
00:12:32.168 --> 00:12:35.129
Has someone threatened you
about your testimony?

181
00:12:36.422 --> 00:12:38.758
The bruises on your face.
did Bryce do that?

182
00:12:38.841 --> 00:12:39.676
No.

183
00:12:40.802 --> 00:12:42.053
Are you afraid of him?

184
00:12:44.430 --> 00:12:45.473
Not a goddamn bit.

185
00:12:51.062 --> 00:12:53.356
- What the fuck did you do. man?
- Whoa. what's wrong?

186
00:12:53.439 --> 00:12:54.273
What's wrong?

187
00:12:54.482 --> 00:12:55.525
- This is wrong.
- What?

188
00:12:55.692 --> 00:12:57.944
Now they'll know we're not weak.
It's totally punk. right?

189
00:12:58.027 --> 00:13:00.571
It's not punk. It's... It's fucking stupid!

190
00:13:01.447 --> 00:13:05.743
- We're in so much trouble right now.
- Who cares? Fuck the system.

191
00:13:05.827 --> 00:13:08.413
"Fuck the..." My dad is gonna kill me.

192
00:13:08.496 --> 00:13:10.415
He won't. Your dad's cool.

193
00:13:10.623 --> 00:13:14.502
- Not with me getting expelled.
- Okay. so we'll get expelled together.

194
00:13:14.585 --> 00:13:16.754
It doesn't have to stop us.

195
00:13:16.963 --> 00:13:18.047
Stop us from doing what?

196
00:13:19.465 --> 00:13:20.925
From bringing down the system.

197
00:13:22.468 --> 00:13:24.595
Those guns? I have more.

198
00:13:24.971 --> 00:13:26.806
We can really make shit happen.

199
00:13:27.724 --> 00:13:29.976
Like you said.
we can end those motherfuckers.

200
00:13:30.059 --> 00:13:33.771
Dude. that was just me saying shit.
That was just me talking. man.

201
00:13:34.022 --> 00:13:37.233
Are you serious right now?
What the fuck is wrong with you?

202
00:13:39.152 --> 00:13:43.239
I'll tell them it was all me.
I'll do whatever you want.

203
00:13:43.322 --> 00:13:46.743
No. no. it's fine. We're good.

204
00:13:48.494 --> 00:13:49.328
Um...

205
00:13:49.412 --> 00:13:54.042
I think. you know. we shouldn't hang out
until this thing blows over.

206
00:14:01.007 --> 00:14:01.966
Are we still friends?

207
00:14:06.220 --> 00:14:07.055
Totally.

208
00:14:15.021 --> 00:14:18.816
<i>Being friends with him.
it was about loyalty.</i>

209
00:14:19.359 --> 00:14:20.985
<i>But it was also about fear.</i>

210
00:14:23.905 --> 00:14:27.325
And how would you describe
Mr. Walker's relationships with girls?

211
00:14:27.742 --> 00:14:30.244
- Were they fear-based as well?
- Yes. sir.

212
00:14:31.329 --> 00:14:33.289
They were like conquests to him.

213
00:14:33.873 --> 00:14:36.834
He would always brag
about what he'd done with girls.

214
00:14:37.543 --> 00:14:40.254
And then he'd call them sluts
for hooking up with him.

215
00:14:40.338 --> 00:14:43.299
And did he ever mention
an "on again. off again" relationship

216
00:14:43.383 --> 00:14:46.677
- with Hannah Baker to you?
- No. sir. because it never happened.

217
00:14:47.136 --> 00:14:48.096
Maybe they hung out.

218
00:14:48.179 --> 00:14:51.516
but there's no way he would've hooked up
with her and not told me about it.

219
00:14:51.599 --> 00:14:53.643
Because he liked to brag. as you said?

220
00:14:54.227 --> 00:14:55.061
Exactly.

221
00:14:55.937 --> 00:14:57.271
How would you describe Hannah?

222
00:14:57.939 --> 00:15:00.274
She was really kind and funny.

223
00:15:01.234 --> 00:15:02.819
Ah!

224
00:15:03.569 --> 00:15:05.822
<i>I liked her
from the first time I saw her.</i>

225
00:15:07.240 --> 00:15:11.828
<i>We only had one real date.
but it was... it was nice.</i>

226
00:15:12.453 --> 00:15:13.621
Fuck you!

227
00:15:13.704 --> 00:15:16.749
<i>I walked her home.
then I went home.</i>

228
00:15:16.833 --> 00:15:18.584
<i>But I couldn't sleep.</i>

229
00:15:18.668 --> 00:15:20.086
Yes. I got you. Okay.

230
00:15:22.130 --> 00:15:24.173
Why don't you take care of that?
Why don't...

231
00:15:24.257 --> 00:15:27.468
<i>And I got in. like. a fight
with my mom's boyfriend.</i>

232
00:15:27.552 --> 00:15:29.846
Oh. yeah.

233
00:15:29.929 --> 00:15:32.265
<i>I texted Hannah.
and she said to come over.</i>

234
00:15:32.348 --> 00:15:34.934
Jesus. Are you sure
you don't want me to call someone?

235
00:15:35.017 --> 00:15:36.769
Yeah. It'll run its course.

236
00:15:38.729 --> 00:15:41.357
Seth will get sick of my mom.
He'll eventually take off.

237
00:15:41.858 --> 00:15:42.859
They usually do.

238
00:15:45.069 --> 00:15:46.154
And what if he doesn't?

239
00:15:49.407 --> 00:15:53.828
Then it gives me more of a reason
to escape to your house. right?

240
00:15:57.665 --> 00:16:00.251
- Thanks. by the way.
- Oh. sure.

241
00:16:02.503 --> 00:16:06.215
So. uh. this is my room.

242
00:16:07.133 --> 00:16:09.510
I was kind of saving it
for our third or fourth date. but...

243
00:16:09.594 --> 00:16:11.137
Shit.

244
00:16:11.471 --> 00:16:15.224
I usually try to save
the whole "my mom's an addict" thing

245
00:16:15.308 --> 00:16:17.518
till the fourth date. too. so...

246
00:16:20.062 --> 00:16:20.897
