00:31:26.259 --> 00:31:27.636
- Oh. shit.
- Whoa.

490
00:31:28.595 --> 00:31:29.763
Hey. Alex.

491
00:31:30.597 --> 00:31:33.517
- Alex. where'd you get that gun?
- Monty gave it to me.

492
00:31:41.024 --> 00:31:43.193
Okay. All right.

493
00:31:44.194 --> 00:31:45.737
Yeah. I'll give you the Polaroids.

494
00:31:46.321 --> 00:31:48.407
And then I'm clean. That's the deal.

495
00:31:53.537 --> 00:31:55.872
Fine. So hand them over.

496
00:31:56.790 --> 00:31:59.668
- I have to get them. They're not here.
- I'll go with you.

497
00:31:59.751 --> 00:32:02.462
- Alex.
- No. I go with him.

498
00:32:07.134 --> 00:32:07.968
Kevin.

499
00:32:11.430 --> 00:32:17.227
So. uh. the district
has completed its review.

500
00:32:17.727 --> 00:32:21.898
and. uh. they've decided
to terminate your employment.

501
00:32:22.107 --> 00:32:23.400
Effective immediately.

502
00:32:38.623 --> 00:32:39.458
Anything else?

503
00:32:40.000 --> 00:32:41.626
If there's anything I can do...

504
00:32:45.630 --> 00:32:48.258
Well. that's very nice. Thank you.

505
00:32:50.010 --> 00:32:53.263
You know what you can do?
You can do more.

506
00:32:53.597 --> 00:32:56.558
These kids. they deserve better
than what we're offering.

507
00:32:56.641 --> 00:33:00.103
- Well. our per-student spending. it's...
- Save the talking points.

508
00:33:00.729 --> 00:33:04.858
You pay that fucker. Coach Rick.
two times more than you pay any counselor.

509
00:33:06.026 --> 00:33:06.860
I made a mistake.

510
00:33:07.652 --> 00:33:09.154
A terrible. tragic mistake.

511
00:33:10.572 --> 00:33:13.909
And maybe
I wasn't trained well enough

512
00:33:13.992 --> 00:33:15.702
for the job that I was asked to do.

513
00:33:16.578 --> 00:33:18.205
Maybe I didn't fit in here either.

514
00:33:19.623 --> 00:33:20.832
Well. I'll take the blame.

515
00:33:21.917 --> 00:33:26.129
- But who's gonna take the blame next time?
- I hope there won't be a next time.

516
00:33:26.213 --> 00:33:29.090
I hope so. too.
but there's always a next time.

517
00:33:38.016 --> 00:33:40.936
These kids. I flagged as most critical.

518
00:33:42.062 --> 00:33:44.940
They need your attention every week.
if not every day.

519
00:33:47.984 --> 00:33:49.611
Or there will be a next time.

520
00:34:12.425 --> 00:34:14.678
<i>I held onto my friendship
with Bryce</i>

521
00:34:15.637 --> 00:34:17.931
<i>because I didn't think
I had anything else.</i>

522
00:34:21.518 --> 00:34:23.144
You went a long way for Bryce.

523
00:34:24.271 --> 00:34:26.606
He'd sell you out to save his own ass
in a heartbeat.

524
00:34:26.690 --> 00:34:28.608
- You know that. right?
- Know what I got. Alex?

525
00:34:28.692 --> 00:34:30.986
I got my friends. I got the team.
That's it.

526
00:34:31.319 --> 00:34:34.781
I don't get to be all sad.
Boo-hoo. my friend died.

527
00:34:34.864 --> 00:34:37.742
I'm gonna put a bullet in my head
so the world feels sorry for me.

528
00:34:40.537 --> 00:34:43.540
Jesus. you wave that gun around
like I give a shit. I don't. man.

529
00:34:45.166 --> 00:34:50.255
If I sell out Bryce or lie.
either way. my whole life falls apart.

530
00:34:51.006 --> 00:34:52.424
I got no one else on my side.

531
00:34:52.841 --> 00:34:54.634
I can't run home. That team's my home.

532
00:34:56.595 --> 00:34:59.097
Going to playoffs. winning state.
being an athlete.

533
00:34:59.180 --> 00:35:00.557
that's not about fun for me.

534
00:35:00.932 --> 00:35:01.975
It's about survival.

535
00:35:02.559 --> 00:35:04.227
It's all I got. It's everything.

536
00:35:04.936 --> 00:35:06.688
So you wanna shoot me? Shoot me.

537
00:35:07.439 --> 00:35:11.401
- Where are the pictures?
- Man. I don't know. I don't have them.

538
00:35:11.610 --> 00:35:14.070
- What?
- I said what I did to get out of there.

539
00:35:15.572 --> 00:35:19.034
'Cause you're not gonna shoot me. Alex.
You can't even shoot yourself.

540
00:35:19.117 --> 00:35:20.243
Fuck you!

541
00:35:29.628 --> 00:35:32.339
By the time you get anywhere.
I'll be long gone.

542
00:35:35.342 --> 00:35:36.384
Is he really worth it?

543
00:35:37.677 --> 00:35:40.513
You're the one with the hole in your head.
You tell me.

544
00:35:47.437 --> 00:35:49.314
<i>I thought Bryce was all I had.</i>

545
00:35:50.649 --> 00:35:52.359
I've texted you. like. 20 times.

546
00:35:53.860 --> 00:35:54.694
Oh.

547
00:35:56.279 --> 00:35:57.447
Missed it. I guess.

548
00:36:00.784 --> 00:36:02.243
I just got a warning.

549
00:36:03.286 --> 00:36:05.038
I told them I should get suspended.

550
00:36:06.081 --> 00:36:07.540
That nothing was your fault.

551
00:36:12.545 --> 00:36:13.421
Are you okay?

552
00:36:20.220 --> 00:36:22.180
You feel safe with me. right?

553
00:36:24.057 --> 00:36:25.058
Of course I do.

554
00:36:26.434 --> 00:36:27.477
And you believe me?

555
00:36:28.269 --> 00:36:30.522
- Bryce...
- Do you believe me? Yes or no?

556
00:36:32.732 --> 00:36:33.650
I believe you.

557
00:36:38.071 --> 00:36:39.531
I'm... I'm a good person.

558
00:36:41.241 --> 00:36:42.325
I know you are.

559
00:36:44.452 --> 00:36:45.286
Do you?

560
00:36:46.663 --> 00:36:50.250
- You really think that?
- Yes. That's why I'm here.

561
00:37:04.514 --> 00:37:05.890
You know I love you. right?

562
00:37:08.351 --> 00:37:09.185
I know.

563
00:37:12.689 --> 00:37:13.857
Tell me you love me.

564
00:37:15.567 --> 00:37:16.401
I do.

565
00:37:17.861 --> 00:37:18.737
I love you.

566
00:37:21.197 --> 00:37:22.031
Good.

567
00:37:24.826 --> 00:37:27.996
<i>But real friends
will give you the bad news.</i>

568
00:37:30.457 --> 00:37:34.127
- Okay. don't freak out.
- Don't start that way and I won't.

569
00:37:34.794 --> 00:37:36.880
- Monty doesn't have the pictures.
- What?

570
00:37:36.963 --> 00:37:38.673
And he lied to us and he ditched me.

571
00:37:38.757 --> 00:37:40.300
And I'm so sorry.

572
00:37:40.717 --> 00:37:42.677
I so wanted the pictures to be the answer.

573
00:37:43.845 --> 00:37:46.181
I tried. Jess. I really tried.

574
00:37:47.932 --> 00:37:51.811
I only wanted this to be okay for you
and to never have to think about it again.

575
00:37:51.895 --> 00:37:52.812
I know.

576
00:37:52.896 --> 00:37:54.647
And this is not our place to say.

577
00:37:55.023 --> 00:37:57.567
I get that.
And... And we shouldn't even be here.

578
00:37:58.026 --> 00:38:00.320
But. look. it's different now.

579
00:38:01.321 --> 00:38:03.114
With those pictures out there somewhere.

580
00:38:03.198 --> 00:38:05.408
all those girls need someone
to stand up for them.

581
00:38:06.201 --> 00:38:08.661
We don't have the pictures.
so we need you.

582
00:38:09.287 --> 00:38:12.165
And we get that you're afraid
that people won't believe you

583
00:38:12.248 --> 00:38:14.834
or that they'll come after you.
and that is so fair.

584
00:38:15.877 --> 00:38:19.255
But we just wanted you to know
that we'll stand by you.

585
00:38:19.506 --> 00:38:20.507
We believe you.

586
00:38:21.674 --> 00:38:22.509
All of us.

587
00:38:34.729 --> 00:38:37.899
Six months ago. I told you
I'd burn Hannah's tapes for you.

588
00:38:37.982 --> 00:38:39.317
and you told me not to.

589
00:38:40.109 --> 00:38:42.403
Because you knew
her story needed to be heard.

590
00:38:43.404 --> 00:38:44.531
And so does yours.

591
00:38:46.491 --> 00:38:48.409
And you don't have to be afraid anymore.

592
00:38:48.493 --> 00:38:52.163
And as lonely as it is.
you'll never be alone.

593
00:38:54.415 --> 00:38:56.584
I told him not to say that
because it's cheesy.

594
00:38:56.793 --> 00:38:58.920
But the point is...

595
00:39:00.129 --> 00:39:02.841
whenever you're ready. we are. too.

596
00:39:05.176 --> 00:39:08.596
If I do this. everything changes.

597
00:39:11.432 --> 00:39:12.684
Maybe it needs to change.

598
00:39:17.272 --> 00:39:19.607
How could you tell
he was assaulting her?

599
00:39:20.441 --> 00:39:24.529
I could tell
because he was standing over her.

600
00:39:24.821 --> 00:39:26.489
- He was just standing over her?
- No.

601
00:39:27.240 --> 00:39:29.075
Well. you gotta be clear about this. son.

602
00:39:30.869 --> 00:39:32.495
He was on top of her. and his...

603
00:39:35.707 --> 00:39:39.377
his penis was out and he was hard.

604
00:39:41.087 --> 00:39:42.088
She wasn't moving.

605
00:39:44.757 --> 00:39:45.758
<i>I. um...</i>

606
00:39:47.176 --> 00:39:48.720
I remember...

607
00:39:51.472 --> 00:39:54.309
seeing him on top of me.

608
00:40:00.565 --> 00:40:05.612
I remember feeling his body crushing me.

609
00:40:09.741 --> 00:40:15.496
I remember him holding me down
and forcing himself on me.

610
00:40:21.878 --> 00:40:23.254
I remember his face.

611
00:40:26.090 --> 00:40:27.926
It was... It was Bryce Walker.

612
00:41:12.387 --> 00:41:13.471
I'm so proud of you.

613
00:41:15.431 --> 00:41:17.600
Thank you.

614
00:41:28.194 --> 00:41:29.487
I never liked you.

615
00:41:30.113 --> 00:41:32.115
- I know.
- And I can never forgive you.

616
00:41:32.615 --> 00:41:33.741
Dad. be nice.

617
00:41:35.368 --> 00:41:38.204
Despite everything.
I thank you for your courage

618
00:41:39.372 --> 00:41:41.290
and wish you children of your own someday

619
00:41:42.333 --> 00:41:45.169
so you'll know what it's like
to wanna save them from the world.

620
00:42:21.497 --> 00:42:25.126
<i>The thing we're all
most afraid of is losing our friends.</i>

621
00:42:26.127 --> 00:42:27.336
<i>is being all alone.</i>

622
00:42:51.277 --> 00:42:54.906
<i>I couldn't wait for the verdict.
so I came to help you with the store.</i>

623
00:42:56.365 --> 00:42:59.702
You know. I didn't realize that.
ah. these things move.

624
00:43:00.286 --> 00:43:01.704
They flipped over everything.

625
00:43:01.788 --> 00:43:03.915
All the shelves.
the computers in the back.

626
00:43:04.582 --> 00:43:08.669
Still. everything's done
and pretty much back in place.

627
00:43:18.054 --> 00:43:18.888
Olivia.

628
00:43:26.938 --> 00:43:28.689
I wonder how long it's been back there.

629
00:43:48.167 --> 00:43:50.419
It still smells like her.

630
00:43:54.382 --> 00:43:57.135
The jury's gonna do the right thing.
I know they will.

631
00:44:00.221 --> 00:44:02.765
<i>No! No!</i>

632
00:44:02.974 --> 00:44:04.976
<i>Not you!</i>

633
00:44:05.476 --> 00:44:07.395
<i>Not my beloved bride!</i>

634
00:44:08.688 --> 00:44:11.149
<i>I'm sorry!</i>

635
00:44:11.941 --> 00:44:14.193
This is a zombie movie.

636
00:44:16.028 --> 00:44:16.863
Yes.

637
00:44:19.532 --> 00:44:21.033
You hate zombie movies.

638
00:44:22.910 --> 00:44:24.245
Yes.

639
00:44:24.662 --> 00:44:27.707
But I couldn't just sit around
waiting for the jury to come back.

640
00:44:27.790 --> 00:44:34.088
And it was this. or a romantic comedy.
or a cancer movie. or something French.

641
00:44:34.630 --> 00:44:35.464
so...

642
00:44:36.841 --> 00:44:39.385
We used to judge people
who came to the movies alone.

643
00:44:41.888 --> 00:44:43.222
Well. I'm not alone. am I?

644
00:44:50.980 --> 00:44:53.357
I think zombies
just really wanna be loved.

645
00:44:55.568 --> 00:44:56.527
That's ridiculous.

646
00:44:57.904 --> 00:45:00.239
Zombies wanna eat brains. That's it.

647
00:45:00.406 --> 00:45:05.286
Period. No deeper meaning.
no metaphor for human existence. nothing.

648
00:45:07.288 --> 00:45:09.290
Except the dead come back to life.

649
00:45:20.760 --> 00:45:22.220
I can't forgive you. Hannah.

650
00:45:25.348 --> 00:45:26.474
I can't ever forgive you.

651
00:45:38.903 --> 00:45:42.365
I was just gonna walk away.
so you didn't have to.

652
00:45:42.448 --> 00:45:44.367
What made you think
I was gonna walk away?

653
00:45:45.326 --> 00:45:47.036
- Don't you think you should?
- No.

654
00:45:49.372 --> 00:45:52.500
I mean. the man was in a coma. For days.

655
00:45:54.669 --> 00:45:56.045
I know.

656
00:45:56.921 --> 00:45:59.840
When I saw him the other night.
I panicked and ran away.

657
00:46:06.138 --> 00:46:07.265
I'm done running.

658
00:46:10.893 --> 00:46:13.312
And if you're gonna know me.
then you need to know all of me.

659
00:46:13.396 --> 00:46:14.397
Yeah. Well. thank you.

660
00:46:21.112 --> 00:46:22.446
My dad got me into boxing.

661
00:46:25.324 --> 00:46:27.868
And I was a fighter
long before I figured out I was gay.

662
00:46:30.037 --> 00:46:32.415
After I figured out I was gay.
I was glad I was a boxer.

663
00:46:34.041 --> 00:46:34.875
I hear that.

664
00:46:37.545 --> 00:46:40.923
And I was glad I was past the point that
my dad could scare the shit out of me.

665
00:46:43.467 --> 00:46:45.136
'Cause I didn't ever
wanna be scared again.

666
00:46:49.306 --> 00:46:50.933
Especially of someone that I love.

667
00:46:57.565 --> 00:46:58.566
It's a backup date?

668
00:47:03.654 --> 00:47:06.657
It's the verdict. I gotta go.

669
00:47:36.228 --> 00:47:37.104
All rise.

670
00:47:41.942 --> 00:47:44.028
The Honorable Judge Martin Campbell
presiding.

671
00:47:50.701 --> 00:47:51.535
Be seated.

672
00:47:56.999 --> 00:47:58.584
Bailiff. bring in the jury. please.

673
00:48:30.157 --> 00:48:32.076
Madam Forewoman.
have you reached a verdict?

674
00:48:32.827 --> 00:48:33.744
We have. Your Honor.

675
00:49:01.981 --> 00:49:03.023
What say you?

676
00:49:06.944 --> 00:49:09.822
We the jury. in the case
of Andrew and Olivia Baker

677
00:49:09.905 --> 00:49:12.408
versus the Evergreen County
School District.

678
00:49:14.410 --> 00:49:16.495
find the defendant not responsible.

679
00:49:21.584 --> 00:49:23.502
Come to order.

680
00:49:26.380 --> 00:49:28.883
Thank you. litigators.
and thank you. jury.

681
00:49:28.966 --> 00:49:33.554
for your patience. deliberation.
and service during this proceeding.

682
00:49:34.013 --> 00:49:36.015
This court is adjourned.

683
00:49:52.281 --> 00:49:54.658
My daughter wasn't the perfect victim.

684
00:49:56.744 --> 00:49:57.912
There's no such thing.

685
00:49:58.662 --> 00:50:02.041
Hannah was a beautiful young woman.

686
00:50:03.250 --> 00:50:09.340
Full of life. and dreams. and passions.
and fears. and failings

687
00:50:09.423 --> 00:50:10.925
like any other teenage girl.

688
00:50:13.677 --> 00:50:14.678
And we let her down.

689
00:50:17.848 --> 00:50:22.853
And people wanna point to the parents.
but we didn't allow her to be bullied.

690
00:50:22.937 --> 00:50:26.732
and we didn't send her away
when she came and asked for help.

691
00:50:26.815 --> 00:50:30.653
and we didn't send her back to class
with her rapist.

692
00:50:33.280 --> 00:50:35.491
Boys bullied her and adults allowed it.

693
00:50:39.036 --> 00:50:40.037
You know. I don't know...

694
00:50:41.330 --> 00:50:47.378
a single woman who hasn't faced
sexual assault. abuse. or worse.

695
00:50:48.587 --> 00:50:49.421
Not one.

696
00:50:53.133 --> 00:50:54.218
Many survive.

697
00:50:55.844 --> 00:50:58.555
My daughter didn't.
and that's not her fault.

698
00:51:00.182 --> 00:51:02.685
Obviously. we are very disappointed
with today's verdict.

699
00:51:03.435 --> 00:51:05.187
We presented a case that we believe in.

700
00:51:06.522 --> 00:51:10.359
But despite today's outcome. we hope
we've sent a message to all schools

701
00:51:11.610 --> 00:51:13.445
that they must do better...

702
00:51:13.821 --> 00:51:15.489
...and that this cannot happen again.

703
00:51:15.823 --> 00:51:18.742
- Students deserve to feel safe.
- Fucking Bryce.

704
00:51:19.201 --> 00:51:20.869
We hope in the near future...

705
00:51:21.245 --> 00:51:22.538
- Bryce Walker?
- Yes. sir?

706
00:51:22.621 --> 00:51:24.498
You're under arrest
for felony sexual assault.

707
00:51:25.124 --> 00:51:27.501
- Excuse me...
- No. You can see him at the station.

708
00:51:28.127 --> 00:51:29.920
- Clear a path. please.
- Clear a path.

709
00:51:30.004 --> 00:51:32.339
Let's go. folks.
We need to get through.

710
00:51:32.881 --> 00:51:34.883
You're making a big fucking mistake.

711
00:51:36.176 --> 00:51:37.970
- Justin Foley. you're under arrest...
- What?

712
00:51:38.053 --> 00:51:39.888
...as an accessory
to felony sexual assault.

713
00:51:39.972 --> 00:51:41.098
Clay. what's going on?

714
00:51:41.181 --> 00:51:42.141
Justin...

715
00:51:43.767 --> 00:51:44.727
Mom? Mom?

716
00:51:45.227 --> 00:51:46.145
Justin! Wait. no.

717
00:51:46.520 --> 00:51:48.314
- Jess. it's okay.
- What?

718
00:51:48.689 --> 00:51:49.523
It's okay.

719
00:51:50.024 --> 00:51:52.443
<i>Friendship is about sacrifice.</i>

720
00:51:52.526 --> 00:51:55.237
- Mom. they-they arrested Justin.
- I know. honey.

721
00:51:55.362 --> 00:51:58.240
Justin knew that was a risk.
going on record about what happened.

722
00:51:58.324 --> 00:52:01.160
Mom. he... He saved my life.

723
00:52:01.827 --> 00:52:03.245
All right? We have to help him.

724
00:52:03.454 --> 00:52:04.288
We will.

725
00:52:04.913 --> 00:52:05.748
I promise.

726
00:52:13.047 --> 00:52:13.881
Jessica.

727
00:52:14.631 --> 00:52:15.966
We got him. We got Bryce.

728
00:52:16.675 --> 00:52:17.968
But they got Justin. too.

729
00:52:20.054 --> 00:52:21.722
What do we do?

730
00:52:24.099 --> 00:52:25.059
You keep fighting.

731
00:52:59.009 --> 00:53:00.886
<i>For help finding crisis resources.</i>

732
00:53:00.969 --> 00:53:02.971
<i>visit 13reasonswhy.info.</i>

